INSTALL — Anteater Poker Alpha
Team 23 | EECS 22L | UCI

DEPENDENCIES
------------
  - GCC (C99 or later)
  - GTK+3 development libraries
  - POSIX threads (pthreads) — included with glibc on Linux
  - GNU Make
  - pkg-config

On the EECS Linux servers (bondi, crystalcove, etc.) these are
already available. On a fresh Ubuntu/Debian machine:

  sudo apt-get install gcc make libgtk-3-dev pkg-config

BUILDING FROM SOURCE
--------------------
  1. Unpack the source archive:
       gtar xvzf Poker_Alpha_src.tar.gz

  2. Enter the project directory:
       cd poker

  3. Build all executables:
       make

     Executables are placed in poker/bin/:
       poker/bin/poker_server
       poker/bin/poker_client

  4. Run unit tests:
       make test

  5. Clean build artifacts:
       make clean

RUNNING (BINARY RELEASE)
-------------------------
  1. Unpack the binary archive:
       gtar xvzf Poker_Alpha.tar.gz

  2. Read the user manual:
       evince poker/doc/Poker_UserManual.pdf

  3. Start the server (background):
       poker/bin/poker_server &

  4. Launch the client:
       poker/bin/poker_client

CUSTOM PORT
-----------
  poker/bin/poker_server 9001 &
  (clients should enter port 9001 on the login screen)

NETWORK PLAY
------------
  - Run poker_server on one machine.
  - Each player runs poker_client on their machine.
  - Enter the server machine's IP address on the login screen.
  - Ensure port 9000 (or your chosen port) is not blocked by a firewall.

UNINSTALLING
------------
  pkill poker_server
  pkill poker_client
  rm -rf poker/
